{"t": 48.94, "n": 49, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I added a test row for ECC-AC5 to `docs/plans/i21.plan.md`. Nothing has been run: this step has no shell, and the new test doesn't exist yet.\n\n**Cause:** this change edits ECC-B13 to list P-CC-13. ECC-AC5 (ECC-B6, ECC-B13, ECC-B14) says the probe results are recorded for the CLI version. No test in `tests/` carried that id. Only `test_task_ac5_...` tests exist, and those belong to an older task's AC 5.\n\n**Edits, all in place:**\n- **Status:** back to `planned`, because the plan changed.\n- **Section 0:** a trip-back note says why the row was added.\n- **R7:** now names ECC-AC5 and states that every probe marked `confirmed` has a dated result row in the runbook with its CLI version, which the facts string in `executor_compat.json` also names.\n- **New row 3.8 (test, R7, proves ECC-AC5):** `test_ecc_ac5_every_confirmed_probe_is_recorded_with_a_date_and_the_cli_version` in `plugins/tempergraph/engine/tests/test_live_checks_mcp_probe.py`.\n  - It reads `LIVE_FACTS` and, for each `confirmed` probe, finds its runbook L-row.\n  - It then checks that section 4 has exactly one result row for it with a date, a CLI version and `passed`.\n  - It also checks that the `executor_compat.json` facts string names that probe and version, and that no `not run` probe appears there as `confirmed`.\n  - With P-CC-13 the only confirmed probe, it passes on L-43, 2026-11-25 and `2.1.332`.\n\nThe existing rows keep their `✓` marks. Row 3.8's Completed cell is empty. The plan stays `complex`, and the verification commands and proof table are unchanged: the new test runs in the second command, `tests/test_live_checks_mcp_probe.py`.\n\nI did not change `executor_compat.json`'s `recorded` or `range`, which still read `2.1.329` while P-CC-13 was confirmed on `2.1.332`. The test deliberately checks only for a dated result row with a CLI version and does not compare that version to the pinned one.\n\nARTIFACT plan: docs/plans/i21.plan.md